<div class="note"><strong>Protocol verification update:</strong> Karting Victoria identifies the Karting Australia CMS as the archive for historical race-meeting results back to 2009. I located the official CMS entry point, but its historical result pages did not load reliably in this research session. Therefore, I have not copied unverified qualifying, heat, pre-final or final positions into the archive. The Victorian Open row above is an official pre-entry record only: it confirms Oscar was entered in Rookies, not that he started or finished in a particular position. <a class="source" href="https://cms.karting.net.au/cms/results/view" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open Karting Australia CMS results ↗</a></div>
<div class="note"><strong>How to read this:</strong> The OGKRC Class Titles and Junior Sprint Classic articles publish top-three lists, placing Oscar first. The club-day reports describe heat-by-heat racing and, where explicitly stated, the overall points result. These are club-event records, not a complete national championship classification. Dates are shown as published by the source; where the report gives only a month, the exact day is not inferred.</div>
